    {
      "id": "1077f4e1cac755a5ee8f58a04195e5ea4846058b",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 471272422,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "They are running with 'tee' and their outputs are added as artifact files.  Their console output is in the raw log, but because the 'conflict' build is so long, the normal view of the log is truncated and they don't show there.\n\nI think the output from the scripts is reasonable (there is nothing to see in this run because there were no changed dissectors to check).  To make them more visible, could we maybe reduce the output from the checkout build?  The other option is returning error codes if issues are seen (I assume this would stop the pipeline and make the errors very visible), which might be harsh for check_typed_item_calls.py, which still flags around 100 proto_tree_add_item() calls.\n\nI think I'd like to merge as-is and watch it for a while, then consider making the scripts return errors when they find something.\n\nAn alternative place to check these could be the commithook...",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
